:: Widgets DoLX Changelog [widget]
<<widget "DoLXChangelog">>
	<div class="changelog-overlay">
		<div class="changelog-hero">
			<span class="changelog-hero-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128220;</span>
			<div>
				<div class="changelog-label">PATCH NOTES</div>
				<h1>DoL X-Change <span>v0.22.2</span></h1>
				<div class="changelog-apk-note"><strong>Official X-Change APK:</strong> Join the DoL Modding server and check the dedicated <a href="https://discord.com/channels/675158131688603721/1512272787572785162" target="_blank">X-Change Channel</a>.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<a class="changelog-release-link" href="https://gitgud.io/Akoz/dol-xchange/-/releases" target="_blank"><span aria-hidden="true">&#128279;</span> View the full changelog and all releases <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon new" aria-hidden="true">&#10022;</span> Changes and Additions</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Updated Vanilla to 0.5.12.13</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Outbreak, a new minigame</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Create a pathogen and spread it before the cure stops you.
			</li>
			<li>Choose a <strong>pathogen, difficulty, name, starting region, and starting traits</strong> before each run.
			</li>
			<li>Added five unlockable pathogens with different playstyles:
				<ul>
				<li><strong>Bacteria</strong>: balanced and straightforward.
				</li>
				<li><strong>Virus</strong>: can mutate and gain free evolutions.
				</li>
				<li><strong>Fungus</strong>: poor regional spread but can use limited <strong>Spore Bursts</strong>.
				</li>
				<li><strong>Parasite</strong>: spreads quietly and can temporarily <strong>Suppress</strong>.
				</li>
				<li><strong>Prion</strong>: starts slowly but gains cure resistance through <strong>Entrenchment</strong>.
				</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li>Main-game rewards include small <strong>Science</strong> rewards, a random <strong>SWP Anti-pill</strong> for winning, or a regular Gray <strong>X-Change pill</strong> for losing, with daily limits.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded Underground Colosseum</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Winners can now breed the loser after a fight.
			</li>
			<li>Children from these fights are raised by the house instead of Bailey's orphanage.
			</li>
			<li>Refusing to breed causes the player to be thrown out and banned.
			</li>
			<li>Added a new-fighter chant and receptionist, goon trials, a Purple pill swap, audience cameos, a cow-transformation hint, and receptionist pregnancy-test dialogue.
			</li>
			<li>Added pub and brothel events for people previously bred by the player, including opportunities to help them.
			</li>
			<li>The receptionist can also appear at the brothel.
			</li>
			<li>Win points now gain a small bonus from Fame and children sired.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Colosseum titles and arena reputation</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>The reputation box now shows the player's Colosseum title, including custom titles.
			</li>
			<li>At <strong>4,000 Combat Fame</strong>, city danger-roll chances are reduced by 15%.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated arena bans and reinstatement</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Talk to Silver Stranger's help for it with the costs <strong>£100,000</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>The arena name resets to <strong>Knife</strong>, while rank and previous fight history remain.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Impregnation Fame display</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Impregnation Fame now has its own correctly labelled row beside Pregnancy Fame.
			</li>
			<li>The row remains visible even at 0 points.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Kylar relationship option</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>The player can ask Kylar to stop telling people they are together.
			</li>
			<li>Kylar may agree or refuse.
			</li>
			<li>If Kylar agrees, they stop announcing the relationship in school hallways.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added two pet-care upgrades</strong>
			<ul>
			<li><strong>Feeding Alarm (£150)</strong> is available at the pet shop and warns two days before parasites would starve.
			</li>
			<li><strong>Console Alert Light (£30)</strong> is available at the arcade prize counter and requires a console.
			</li>
			<li>It flashes when the virtual pet needs care, is under attack, or has a boss fight waiting.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded clothing</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Added dotted panties to the clothing shop, with art by <strong>nicos</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Added the <strong>Silky</strong> clothing trait.
			</li>
			<li>Silky clothing prevents nipple/genital rubbing messages and Arousal from clothing.
			</li>
			<li>Silky can be disabled under <strong>Settings &gt; Modded Clothing Traits</strong>.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Leighton changing-room camera sabotage</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>After seeing the hidden-camera photos during Avery's card game, the player can search the school changing rooms at night and attempt to disable the cameras with Skulduggery.
			</li>
			<li>Cameras are replaced after one week.
			</li>
			<li>Leighton investigates during the next Science lesson.
			</li>
			<li>Being caught on camera causes detention.
			</li>
			<li>At low School Status, another student may blame the player even without proof.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added a hospital emergency contact</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>The player can choose who collects them from the hospital through the foyer.
			</li>
			<li>Once close enough, available contacts are Robin, Whitney, Kylar, Sydney, and Avery instead of Bailey.
			</li>
			<li>Each has their own pickup scene.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Avery bath scene</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Returning to the mansion late at night while especially dirty can cause Avery to tell the player to wash before continuing the evening.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added cramps after excessive orgasms</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Reaching 15+ orgasms in one day can cause next-day cramps, Pain, and Fatigue.
			</li>
			<li>Effects become stronger at 20+ orgasms.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded Wren's lap game</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Wren becomes harder to resist as their Arousal rises.
			</li>
			<li>Wren's Arousal now appears with a bar and description.
			</li>
			<li>The player can tease Wren while sitting in their lap, spending Willpower to raise both characters' Arousal and potentially earn larger tips.
			</li>
			<li>If Wren becomes aroused or impatient enough, harsher bets can appear.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Whitney bike-recovery events</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>After the orphanage arc (loft or barge in), Whitney may intervene when the player's bike is stolen.
			</li>
			<li>Depending on the relationship, Whitney may keep it, return it damaged, repair it, or take the player for a ride.
			</li>
			<li>If Whitney cannot appear immediately, the encounter can happen later in town.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded combat/sex encounters</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Added foot-job options such as <strong>Ask for a foot job</strong> and <strong>Ready your face</strong> at climax.
			</li>
			<li>Added chest actions such as <strong>Push towards their mouth</strong> and <strong>Free your chest</strong> during non-consensual fights.
			</li>
			<li>Added automatic condom-breaking chance settings for both the player and NPCs.
			</li>
			<li>NPC condoms can also be damaged with <strong>Damage their condom</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed toy dropping, non-consensual face positioning, stuck foot-job panels, and choke/rough requests being wasted on islanders who cannot understand them.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added new Gwylan, Whitney, and Avery events</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Added Gwylan petplay activities including trick training, hide-and-seek, posing, porch leash waiting, supper, washing/grooming, bedtime, morning reactions, reconciliation, and a summer sunscreen interaction.
			</li>
			<li>Petplay does not require an animal transformation, though animal traits add extra reactions.
			</li>
			<li>Expanded the familiar-collar and pet-bed progression.
			</li>
			<li>Added Whitney school hide-and-seek with Athletics, Skulduggery, chance, romance, and bully variations.
			</li>
			<li>Added Whitney shopping leash scenes for romance and bully routes, including stranger reactions and a romance collar tag.
			</li>
			<li>Added Whitney restraint play at their flat and expanded the forced park dog walk.
			</li>
			<li>Added Avery dog-walk reactions, including a muzzle-shopping sequence after biting the pedestrian.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added new Gender Identity sidebar symbols</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Enable <strong>Show gender symbol in the sidebar</strong>, then choose <strong>Sidebar symbol &gt; Gender identity</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Supports boy, girl, enby, trans boy, trans girl, and trans enby.
			</li>
			<li>Body sex remains the default.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added proper ambience for snow</strong>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Tweaks and Rebalancing</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Improved wardrobe</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Increased wardrobe capacity to <strong>3,500 items</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Added search and Filters for gender, reveal, warmth, and traits.
			</li>
			<li>Added a Help popover explaining wardrobe controls.
			</li>
			<li>Clothing tabs are grouped into <strong>Favorites</strong>, <strong>Body</strong>, <strong>Head &amp; neck</strong>, and <strong>Extras</strong>, with text labels.
			</li>
			<li>Improved phone layout and added icons for the seaweed top and skirt.
			</li>
			<li>Equipped outer garments now each have an explicit <strong>Strip</strong> link beside their name.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Rebalanced preferred-trait Trauma relief</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Preferred traits provide less Trauma relief the longer they remain continuously active.
			</li>
			<li>Relief gradually drops to 10% of the original effect after one week.
			</li>
			<li>Going without the trait for a week restores full Trauma relief.
			</li>
			<li>Stress relief is unchanged.
			</li>
			<li>Can be disabled in Attitudes with <strong>Get used to preferred traits</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Corrected the description of <strong>Gender reactions in same-gender groups</strong> to clarify that it affects Dysphoria/comfort, not Gender Identity.
			</li>
			<li>Attitudes toggle descriptions now use (?) tooltips.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Rebalancing settings</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Added <strong>Combat Stress Gain</strong> under <strong>Modded Settings &gt; Rebalancing</strong>, adjustable from 25% to 150% with 100% as default.
			</li>
			<li>Only affects Stress gained during non-consensual combat.
			</li>
			<li>Combined Maths and History buffs into <strong>Trait Buffs</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Combined Substance, Dancing, and Food Spoilage settings into <strong>Gameplay Rebalances</strong>.
			</li>
			<li><strong>Enable All / Disable All</strong> no longer changes <strong>Easy Housekeeping</strong> under Grind.
			</li>
			<li>Improved Animal TF and History trait tooltips.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Daily Purity descriptions</strong>
			<ul>
			<li><strong>Purity Boost</strong> now clearly says it adds extra Purity each day.
			</li>
			<li><strong>Impurity Boost</strong> now clearly says it removes extra Purity each day.
			</li>
			<li>Either can push the total daily change above or below zero.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated handholding virginity</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Only gloves and mittens protect handholding virginity.
			</li>
			<li>Bracelets, wrist cuffs, and gold shackles no longer count as covering the hands.
			</li>
			<li>Also applies to Bailey and Silly Pregnancy Mode.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Antique Jewellery and Master Baiter requirements</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Antique Jewellery and <strong>Master Baiter</strong> now unlock at 80% museum completion instead of 100%.
			</li>
			<li>Existing saves meeting the threshold unlock automatically.
			</li>
			<li><strong>It Belongs in a Museum</strong> still requires 100%.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Hairdresser stealing</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Night-time stealing is limited to one bottle of hair gel and one hair-growth formula per week.
			</li>
			<li>Both reset weekly.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Daily Purity</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Temporary X-Change bodies no longer incorrectly grant the daily virginity Purity bonus.
			</li>
			<li>Daily Purity now uses the player's true body while temporarily X-Changed.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Fixes and Improvements</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Fixed Seaspray Hotel scenes</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Fixed the dog scene.
			</li>
			<li>Consensual hotel clients no longer start sex scenes already angry.
			</li>
			<li>Rape, fight, and spanking scenes keep their existing Anger behaviour.
			</li>
			<li>Bailey's room and the manager no longer appear before enough hotel work has been completed.
			</li>
			<li>The manager requires some cleaning shifts before the trouble scene can appear.
			</li>
			<li>Bailey's lotus-door room requires 5 shifts.
			</li>
			<li>The front desk now gives the lotus-door warning when the player is hired.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed manager introduction pronouns.
			</li>
			<li>The hotel manager no longer calls the player in immediately after hiring.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Bailey's office</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Fixed office display issues after the Poppy meeting.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed pronoun errors during the orphanage hallway cat pounch.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed dancing UI</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Gave the numbered <strong>Continue</strong> link more room to prevent overlapping dance buttons.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed earrings during undressing</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Earrings stay equipped during ordinary undressing.
			</li>
			<li>School-pool outfit changes no longer send earrings home.
			</li>
			<li>Earrings can still be changed normally through the wardrobe.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed collar handling</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Whitney no longer replaces an existing collar with theirs and waits for it to be removed first.
			</li>
			<li>Chokers can still be replaced.
			</li>
			<li>Kylar's abduction respects all locked collars, including Bailey's, instead of forcing the iron collar.
			</li>
			<li>Chalet clients who cannot remove a locked collar attach a leash to it instead.
			</li>
			<li>Later chalet text reflects the existing collar.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed leash scenes giving the wrong neckwear instead of a collar.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed the Free Use collar punishment incorrectly applying a leash.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated school locker bag handling</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Bags can be stored in the school locker when the player's hands are empty.
			</li>
			<li>Storing a Handheld item no longer stores the bag as well.
			</li>
			<li>Taking a bag out no longer sends the currently worn bag to the wardrobe.
			</li>
			<li>Automatic pre-class take-out handles bags correctly.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed consensual-sex Pain</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Being pinned or teased at the entrance no longer counts as penetration.
			</li>
			<li>Pain only starts building once actual penetration begins.
			</li>
			<li>Cock Addict is no longer satisfied by a penis only touching the entrance.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed custom makeup colours</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Custom eyeshadow, lipstick, and mascara now display the chosen colour instead of a red tint.
			</li>
			<li>Custom blusher no longer turns black.
			</li>
			<li>Custom eyeshadow and lipstick now appear correctly during combat.
			</li>
			<li>Removed <strong>Skip desaturate filter</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Each makeup type now uses the correct rendering behaviour automatically.
			</li>
			<li>Older saves update automatically.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Gentleman's Club envelope outfits</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Maid dress, butler suit, and feather duster outfits now equip correctly.
			</li>
			<li>Missing clothing is skipped instead of stripping the slot and breaking the outfit.
			</li>
			<li>The chastity parasite now attaches correctly.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Move to Handbag with one-piece outfits</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Moving a one-piece outfit no longer pulls bottoms from other matching outfits.
			</li>
			<li>Already broken outfits can be repaired by moving each affected outfit into the handbag and then back to the wardrobe.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed orgasm-during-penetration tracking</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>The stat now counts only orgasms during actual penetration.
			</li>
			<li>Denied orgasms, dreams, and flashbacks no longer count.
			</li>
			<li>Prevents Genital Addict from unlocking too early.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed transformation Physique modifiers</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>TF Stat Rebalance now applies transformation Physique buffs/debuffs correctly:
				<ul>
				<li>Wolf: +20%
				</li>
				<li>Cow: +40%
				</li>
				<li>Bear: +50%
				</li>
				<li>Cat: -20%
				</li>
				<li>Fox: -10%
				</li>
				<li>Bird: -30%
				</li>
				<li>Bunny: -30%
				</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li>Footwear, pregnancy, hallucinogens, White So Pale, and Stat Nerf Physique effects work correctly again.
			</li>
			<li>Maximum Fatigue is unchanged.
			</li>
			<li>Transformation Physique modifiers now appear on the Characteristics screen.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Avery date outfit checks</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Avery now judges the clothes being worn rather than the player's overall presentation.
			</li>
			<li>Valid feminine/masculine outfits are no longer rejected incorrectly.
			</li>
			<li>Avery's date compliment now follows the outfit: masculine = <strong>handsome</strong>, feminine = <strong>beautiful</strong>, otherwise <strong>gorgeous</strong>.
			</li>
			<li>Also fixed on the Valentine's date.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed wardrobe errors with older saves</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Wardrobe, loft reading nook, and tailor no longer error on older saves while certain sex toys are equipped.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Robin's lemonade-stand greeting</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Robin's greeting no longer prints twice at the beach stand.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed morning-after pill with instant conception</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Instantly created pregnancies now remain preventable for the first two days, matching normal conceptions.
			</li>
			<li>The morning-after pill removes them correctly.
			</li>
			<li>Pain depends on how long the player waited.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Bailey desk-warming</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Bailey lap/desk sex now counts for Cock craving.
			</li>
			<li>Prevents the incorrect empty-without-cock Stress orgasm while Bailey is already inside the player.
			</li>
			<li>Kylar's owl now notices desk-warming sex in Bailey's office.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Whitney pill handover</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Whitney now gives the same pill colour shown in dialogue and combat events.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed pronouns and X-Change pill statistics</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Pronoun selection no longer uses Unaccepted sets when no pronouns are marked Preferred.
			</li>
			<li><strong>X-Change pills taken</strong> now counts Pink, Blue, Choice, and custom-made pills correctly.
			</li>
			<li>X-Change spikes from Bailey's unpaid-rent punishment and blackmail quests now count as spikes.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Avery food requests</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Asking Avery to stock a missing ingredient also makes the dish recipe available to learn in the study if it is not already known.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed vibrator virginity and group-toy tracking</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Bullet and wand vibrators no longer take virginity even when <strong>Toys can take virginity</strong> is enabled.
			</li>
			<li>Dildos are unchanged.
			</li>
			<li>Succubus/Incubus characters can feed when a vulva-owning partner orgasms during cunnilingus or tribbing.
			</li>
			<li>Tribbing through a chastity belt does not count.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed toys marking the wrong partner as penetrated in group sex.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed a missing reaction when a partner stops a toy in the player's right hand.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Ivory Wraith tentacle toggle</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Added <strong>Disable Wraith tentacles</strong> under Wraith Mods.
			</li>
			<li>When enabled, the Ivory Wraith uses its multi-armed form instead.
			</li>
			<li>Wraith tentacle stalking events/scenes are disabled.
			</li>
			<li>Tentacles from other creatures are unaffected.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded Gwylan's Avery question</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>During the mansion heist, the player can say they have grown attached to Avery at Love 50+.
			</li>
			<li>Gwylan's response changes depending on whether Avery's rage has already been seen.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Water Dragon hatchlings</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Hatchlings now show as Water Dragons instead of Hawks when naming them.
			</li>
			<li>Includes hatchlings from Harper's lab.
			</li>
			<li>Existing incorrectly saved lab hatchlings repair automatically.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Dragon Baby issues</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Indigo babies use the correct skin colour.
			</li>
			<li>Dragon features retain blue/lilac colours instead of using hair colour.
			</li>
			<li>Nest child no longer disappear or show broken counts.
			</li>
			<li>Interrupted hatching can recover, including affected existing saves.
			</li>
			<li>Restored missing human-toy unlocks.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed paternity and Statistics mismatches with dragon transmutation.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed twin-hatching and eye-colour text mismatches.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Meds cabinet</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Fixed medicine drawer errors caused by history navigation.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed old-save conversion wiping pill stock and automatic-dose settings.
			</li>
			<li>Prescription painkiller wording now matches its pharmacy source.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed weather renderer</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Snow and rain reuse existing canvas and particle data instead of constantly rebuilding them.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed rain splashes constantly replacing particles.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed inactive rain/snow effects surviving refreshes.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed delayed loading bringing back removed weather effects.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed rapid graphics toggling restarting the renderer incorrectly or leaving it unloaded.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Autism locations and assessment</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Temple bunk, Eden's cabin, and wolf cave now support unmasking, focused interests, stimming, and assessment questionnaires.
			</li>
			<li>Temple stimming uses the dressing screen for privacy.
			</li>
			<li>Assessment reports can be shared with Jordan.
			</li>
			<li>These activities are blocked correctly during possession or combat.
			</li>
			<li>Autism data is no longer unnecessarily initialised for characters without the trait.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed genital transformation progression</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Final genital changes no longer require the Identity meter to be almost completely full.
			</li>
			<li>Transformations finish once genital preferences are fully one-sided and the meter is sufficiently toward that side.
			</li>
			<li>Feminisation no longer pauses during pregnancy.
			</li>
			<li>Statistics now matches this behaviour.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Ear Slime chastity parasite image</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>The parasite no longer shows a missing image after genital changes or Ear Slime removal.
			</li>
			<li>Losing the penis while wearing it now causes it to fall off immediately with a message.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed X-Change reverting during vine pregnancy</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Vaginal and anal vine pregnancies now prevent X-Change from wearing off or being reversed.
			</li>
			<li>Updated pill-duration messages.
			</li>
			<li>Identity-driven body changes can no longer bypass pregnancy protection.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Angel's Forgive</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Forgive no longer falsely marks the player's Love Interest as mentioned.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Ambush and clothing-drop options</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Foxes with <strong>Thrill of the Chase</strong> regain missing <strong>Ambush</strong> actions.
			</li>
			<li>Ambush can be used whenever someone is following, not only while they are running.
			</li>
			<li>Clothing-drop stalking options now use shorter labels.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed bait worm count</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Re-bait messages now count only bait worms the player can actually use.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed transformation unlock decay</strong>
			<ul>
			<li>Mirror transformation options disappear again when the transformation naturally fades.
			</li>
			<li>Safe Genome Dump unlocks remain permanent.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed chimeras incorrectly unlocking base transformations.
			</li>
			<li>Fixed Bunny transformation loading issues.
			</li>
			</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
